# Direct dependencies. Floors track the major line the code is written against;
# the exact set that gets installed lives in the generated requirements.txt.
#
# Regenerate after editing — CI recompiles and diffs, so a stale lock fails the
# build instead of shipping quietly. CI takes the Python version from the
# Dockerfile's base image, so keep the two in step:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.14 --universal \
#     --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
#
# --universal: resolve for every platform, not the one that happens to run the
#   command. The image is built for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 while this is
#   usually run on macOS.
# --generate-hashes: the image installs with --require-hashes, so a replaced
#   artifact on PyPI cannot slip into a build.
